    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "COL",
      "chapter": 4,
      "chapter_usfm": "COL.4",
      "version_id": 100,
      "version_abbr": "NASB1995",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "COL.4.1",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Masters, grant to your slaves justice and fairness, knowing that you too have a Master in heaven."
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "COL.4.2",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Devote yourselves to prayer, keeping alert in it with an attitude of thanksgiving;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "COL.4.3",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "praying at the same time for us as well, that God will open up to us a door for the word, so that we may speak forth the mystery of Christ, for which I have also been imprisoned;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "COL.4.4",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "that I may make it clear in the way I ought to speak."
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "COL.4.5",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Conduct yourselves with wisdom toward outsiders, making the most of the opportunity."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "COL.4.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Let your speech always be with grace, as though seasoned with salt, so that you will know how you should respond to each person."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "COL.4.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "As to all my affairs, Tychicus, our beloved brother and faithful servant and fellow bond-servant in the Lord, will bring you information."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "COL.4.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For I have sent him to you for this very purpose, that you may know about our circumstances and that he may encourage your hearts;"
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "COL.4.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and with him Onesimus, our faithful and beloved brother, who is one of your number. They will inform you about the whole situation here."
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "COL.4.10",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Aristarchus, my fellow prisoner, sends you his greetings; and also Barnabas’s cousin Mark (about whom you received instructions; if he comes to you, welcome him);"
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "COL.4.11",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "and also Jesus who is called Justus; these are the only fellow workers for the kingdom of God who are from the circumcision, and they have proved to be an encouragement to me."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "COL.4.12",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Epaphras, who is one of your number, a bondslave of Jesus Christ, sends you his greetings, always laboring earnestly for you in his prayers, that you may stand perfect and fully assured in all the will of God."
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "COL.4.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For I testify for him that he has a deep concern for you and for those who are in Laodicea and Hierapolis."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "COL.4.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Luke, the beloved physician, sends you his greetings, and also Demas."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "COL.4.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Greet the brethren who are in Laodicea and also Nympha and the church that is in her house."
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "COL.4.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "When this letter is read among you, have it also read in the church of the Laodiceans; and you, for your part read my letter that is coming from Laodicea."
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "COL.4.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Say to Archippus, “Take heed to the ministry which you have received in the Lord, that you may fulfill it.”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "COL.4.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I, Paul, write this greeting with my own hand. Remember my imprisonment. Grace be with you."
        }
      ],
      "verse_count": 18,
      "headings": [],
      "footnotes": [
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "COL.4.15",
          "note_ref": "",
          "note_type": "footnote",
          "references": [],
          "text": "Or Nymphas (masc)"
        }
      ],
